data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let $Q(x) = \\mathrm{round}(x/s)\\,s$ be the staircase. You want an output whose value is $Q(x)$ and whose derivative with respect to $x$ is $1$. A term $x + (Q(x) - x)$ has value $Q(x)$. Its derivative is $1 + (Q' - 1)$, and $Q'$ is zero almost everywhere. Detaching the difference removes its contribution to the backward pass."},"hints_note":null}

